# Character workflow

## Creation (one-time)

Players build characters via `PlayerCreationWizard` (desktop). Rulebook refs: `curated/statistics.md` (9 stats, point buy 60–80), `curated/skills.md`, `sections/061-skill-trees.md`.

| Step | Rule | Code |
|------|------|------|
| Stats | Split point-buy across **all 9 stats** (incl. SPD); min 1, max 10 | `characterCreation.ts` → `validateCreationAttributes` |
| Profession package | 44 pts across 11 skills; defining skill = tree core | `professionPackageRefs`, `PROFESSION_PACKAGE_POINTS` |
| Pickup skills | Budget = INT + REF; max 6 at creation | `pickupSkillBudget`, `validatePickupSkills` |
| Finish | Set `creation.complete: true` | locks stats unless DM enables manual edit |

**SPD is a core stat**, not derived. Run (SPD×3) and Leap are derived — see `calcDerivedStats`.

## Profession skill trees

Static per rulebook — **not** editable on the Other tab. Data: `data/skill-trees.json` (generated by `scripts/build-skill-trees.py`). Logic: `skillTrees.ts`. UI: `ProfessionSkillTree` (desktop + player-web).

- Levels stored in `character.professionTree` keyed by ability id (`Bard:core`, `Bard:0:t1`, …)
- Unlock next tier when parent ability ≥ 5 (`TREE_UNLOCK_AT`)
- Legacy `professionAbilities` / `definingSkillLevel` migrated in `normalizeCharacter.ts`

## Progression spending

After `creation.complete`, players spend points themselves; GM awards I.P. / training I.P. via session controls.

| Spend | Cost | Code |
|-------|------|------|
| Skill +1 | current level (×2 if special) | `spendSkillLevel`, `skillRaiseCost` |
| Stat +1 | current level × 10 training I.P. | `spendStatLevel`, `statRaiseCost` |
| Tree ability +1 | same as skill | `spendTreeLevel` |

All player updates go through `validatePlayerProgression` — server enforces on `PUT /api/player/me`.

## Sheet edit modes (player characters)

| Actor | Mode | Behavior |
|-------|------|----------|
| DM, `!creation.complete` | Full edit | Legacy characters — all fields editable |
| DM, `creation.complete` | Session controls | Award level / I.P. / training I.P.; optional **manual edit** toggle for raw edits |
| Player, `creation.complete` | Spend mode | Read-only stats/skills + `SkillSpendButton` / `StatSpendButton` / tree spend |

## UI conventions

- Use shared `Stepper` for numeric +/- (supports press-and-hold repeat until cap or release)
- Desktop components live under `apps/desktop/.../components/`; mirror spend/tree UI in `apps/player-web/` where players need it
- Do not reintroduce flat profession-abilities table on Other tab
